      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لَهُ إِنَّ أَصْحَابَنَا يَرْوُونَ أَنَّ حَلْقَ اَلرَّأْسِ فِي غَيْرِ حَجٍّ وَ لاَ عُمْرَةٍ مُثْلَةٌ فَقَالَ «كَانَ أَبُو اَلْحَسَنِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ إِذَا قَضَى نُسُكَهُ عَدَلَ إِلَى قَرْيَةٍ يُقَالُ لَهَا سَايَةُ فَحَلَقَ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3124 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Bazanti narrated from Abu Al-Hasan (as):\nI said to him, \"Our companions narrate that shaving the head outside of Hajj or Umrah is considered mutilation.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Abu Al-Hasan (as), after completing his rituals, would go to a village called Sāyah and shave his head there.\""
        ]
      }
